course: dictionary
lesson: 8758
title: Seventeen, the number 17
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Seventeen is a number word. It is written 17 in figures, and it comes right after sixteen. If you count on from sixteen, the next number you say is seventeen.
explain: «Theo's brother Marcus is seventeen and plays GTA 6 in the living room.» Here seventeen tells you Marcus's age: he is 17 years old. Numbers like this are also used for prices and scores.
explain: The word can be split into ten and seven. The French name «dix-sept» works the same way: it means ten-seven. Spotting the parts of a number word can help you read and spell bigger numbers.
fact: Seventeen is written 17 in figures.
fact: Seventeen is one more than sixteen.
fact: Seventeen is ten and seven.
fact: Seventeen is a prime number, because only 1 and itself divide it exactly.
fact: «Some American cicadas spend thirteen or seventeen years underground before coming out together.»
exercise: What number is seventeen in figures? | 71 | 7 | *17 | 117
exercise: «Theo's brother Marcus is seventeen.» How old is Marcus? | *17 years old | 7 years old | 1 year old | 70 years old
exercise: Seventeen is one more than which number? | 10 | 15 | *16 | 18
test: Seventeen is ten and seven. Which two numbers make up seventeen in the same way? | Eight and nine | *Ten and seven | Five and five | Twelve and five
test: What is one more than seventeen? | 16 | 19 | 17 | *18
exam: Which statement about seventeen is true? | *Seventeen is a prime number | Seventeen is one less than fifteen | Seventeen is the same as sixteen | Seventeen is an even number
